<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 19.90 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 19.90 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 19.90 percent at an auction on Monday from 22.97 percent at the last auction on April 28, Kazakhstan's National Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The following are details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 12	     Apr 28</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ46K1311971     KZ45K3010977</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  700		  650</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, maln tenge)	3,028		2,970</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 700		  650</p>
<p> Average price			 90.95 pct	  89.70</p>
<p> Average yield			 19.90 pct	  22.97</p>
<p> Tenor				   182 days	   182 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Nov 13, 1997     Oct 30, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
